       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **What was written:** 2400 mg per dose, four times daily, is 9,600 mg/day.\n- **Maximum dose:** The maximum for oral ibuprofen is 3,200 mg/day for prescription use, and usually 800 mg per dose. This order is three times that. It would risk GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nYou may have meant **2400 mg/day total**. That would be **600 mg by mouth four times daily**, which is within the range. Typical regimens are 400\u2013800 mg every 6\u20138 hours as needed, up to 3,200 mg/day.\n\nPlease confirm the dose you want, ideally with your resident or attending. For example, I can enter ibuprofen 600 mg PO four times daily once you confirm. If you really intend 2400 mg per dose, I can't enter it as written."
